# Claude Code agent memory (machine-local)
.claude/projects/

# --- ADR-0067 phase 4: the second committed skill root is now a generated VIEW ------------
# `.agents/skills` is STILL a runtime skill root — both Claude and Codex load it, and it is half of
# the union `<FsggKitSkillRoots>` + `<FsggKitViewSkillRoots>` declares in
# `.config/kit/FS.GG.Kit.receiver.proj`. It is simply no longer a second COMMITTED copy of
# `.claude/skills`: `scripts/skill-view generate` resolves it at checkout (FS-GG/.github#1676, #1760).
#
# It is git-ignored rather than committed because a COMMITTED symlink does not degrade safely: under
# `git -c core.symlinks=false` (the git-for-Windows default without Developer Mode) it checks out as a
# small regular text file, and both runtimes then exit 0 with zero skills and no diagnostic
# (ADR-0067 §6). An untracked generated root fails loudly instead — `scripts/skill-view check`, with
# both its declaration and resolution lanes, runs on the required `skill-view-check` context.
#
# `.claude/skills/skill-manifest.json` deliberately has NO counterpart here: `skill-view generate
# --mode copy` copies `<id>/` skill directories and no top-level files, so the producer manifest lives
# in the tracked source root and is read from there (FS.GG.SDD#771). `scripts/check-root-asymmetry.sh`
# is one-directional for exactly that reason — do not "tidy" it into a symmetric `diff -r`.
#
# Do NOT commit this root, and do NOT delete this line to "fix" a missing directory. Regenerate it:
#   bash scripts/skill-view generate --source .claude/skills --roots ".agents/skills"
/.agents/skills

# FS.GG.SDD — regenerable per-feature readiness output (ADR-0018).
# SDD dogfoods via Spec Kit, so its readiness views land at specs/<id>/readiness/.
# Transient run output: ignore by role, never commit, do not re-include per feature.
# See docs/reference/artifact-taxonomy.md. (Root readiness/ pinned proofs stay committed.)
#
# Exception: the compact merge-boundary verdict is durable-generated (ADR-0026) and IS
# committed. Excluding the directory *contents* (`*/*`) rather than the directory is
# load-bearing: git never descends into an excluded directory, so the negation would
# otherwise be silently inert. Nested agent-commands/<target>/ stays ignored — `*/*`
# matches that directory itself.
specs/*/readiness/*/*
!specs/*/readiness/*/ship-verdict.json
